Read CLAUDE.md in the repository root before changing anything. It contains the
house conventions and the list of failures this project has already had.

The points most often got wrong, repeated here because a rules file is the only
thing some tools read:

- Never edit /var/www/iwopo (live). Work on staging; ship with `iwopo-deploy`.
- vendor_id comes from the JWT, never from a request body. This is a
  multi-tenant app and a leak between vendors is the worst thing that can
  happen to it.
- After any schema change, or any npm install/ci in a backend folder, run
  `npx prisma generate` and restart. A clean install deletes the generated
  Prisma client and the API crash-loops.
- To check live is healthy, hit an API endpoint. Every page returns 200 while
  the API is dead, because nginx serves the SPA.
- `router.get('/:slug')` swallows later single-segment GETs. Check route order.
- No !important outside prefers-reduced-motion. No dead or duplicate CSS.
- Re-run lint after deleting any UI; it orphans handlers.
- Verify the whole round trip, and look at anything visual rather than
  measuring that it exists.

---

For an assistant working from an editor, with no access to the server:

- **You cannot verify anything.** You cannot run `iwopo-verify`, reach either
  database, or test a change. Never call something verified, working or safe —
  say what you changed and what still needs checking on the server.
- **The person directing you is not a developer.** He will not catch a bad
  change by reading the diff. Explain in plain language what a change does and
  what it might break, and say when you are unsure rather than sounding
  confident.
- **Comments that look odd are usually load-bearing.** They explain a failure
  that already happened here. Do not tidy them away or simplify the code they
  are defending.
- **Do not reformat.** No whole-file passes, no reordering imports for
  neatness. `iwopo-deploy` runs a diff-sanity check that treats a large
  unexplained change as a red flag, and a huge diff hides the real one.
- **`VendorPanel.jsx` is very large on purpose for now.** Do not offer to split
  it up as a side quest.
- **Do not add dependencies casually.** One was recently removed for carrying
  two advisories while importing nothing. If a package is needed, say why and
  what it costs.
- **Flag anything touching `prisma/schema.prisma`.** Schema changes need manual
  steps on the server — `npx prisma generate` and a restart on both live and
  staging — that you cannot perform.
- **You cannot deploy.** Your changes sit in the clone until they are pushed,
  and still need `iwopo-deploy` run on the server afterwards. Say so rather
  than implying a change is live.
